Skip stream registers once the controller is reset

The previous patch bounds the stream reset waits, but the cause of the hang it fixed was the order
of `uhda_destroy`. It resets the controller through `UhdaController::suspend` before destroying it.
The destructors of the streams run after that, which expect to get a reset bit set, which is never
the case since the controller has already been reset. 

The streams don't need to the reset, so we set the stream's space to the register base, effectively
skipping its registers.

--- a/src/controller.cpp
+++ b/src/controller.cpp
@@ -65,6 +65,15 @@
 	if (lock) {
 		uhda_kernel_free_spinlock(lock);
 	}
+
+	// The controller is in reset by now, which resets its streams too, so the stream destructors
+	// that run after this must not touch their registers
+	for (auto& stream : in_streams) {
+		stream.space = uhda::MemSpace {0};
+	}
+	for (auto& stream : out_streams) {
+		stream.space = uhda::MemSpace {0};
+	}
 }
 
